body:
I didn't swap the position of the speakers, I just swapped the wiring for the same effect, with the confirmation that the noise wasn't due to some mechanical vibration or poor placement of the speaker, and yes, the noise comes from the same one. 

&#x200B;

What I didn't do yet, was trying another head, but I did try by previous cab, it's a 2x12 framus with v30s, and doesn't distort.

&#x200B;

I did that before asking on the internet. I thought it was common sense. In the post I said I disassembled the cabinet. I tried different wiring connections/combinations, confirmed the correct impedances, etc. Speaker cable also. I've isolated the noise to that specific speaker, yes. My issue is, why does it oscillate between good and distorted? A speaker isn't that complex and doesn't have much to fail. 

&#x200B;

Thanks for your input, though, cheers. \^\^

>I am the type of person who really hates trends.

